ike  part of the context the waterfall  building it was commissioned by  bob rennie um who's like a big developer  here in vancouver and so this was one of  the buildings that  kind of brought his reputation back up i  think it'll be interesting  [Music]  so this building was designed in 1996  and i think it was completed in the  early 2000s  and the concept was basically to  create a sense of community spirit  within these apartments and  he achieved this through this courtyard  so there's four apartment blocks that's  around the courtyard so  there's this one this one  and this one and there's one  right in front that you guys can't see  and there's also this weird  pyramid-shaped  art gallery which is  now used for wedding stuff  and i think the most incredible part of  this  building this courtyard experience is  this waterfall  apparently it was created to  separate the streets from the courtyard  acoustically and this  this curve here  it kind of acts as a sundial  so depending on what time of day or  what season you come to see the  courtyard  the sun angle will change ever so  slightly  [Music]  so these are some of the other functions  there's a hair salon  and a marijuana dispensary and this  was designed as a art gallery but  looks like it's being used for wedding  services now  and the rest of it is basically um  live work studios for artists and  i've only been to one of them once  and it was really really beautiful it's  like  16 foot tall faces like  light from both directions i think all  the units are  interlocking so you get sun exposure  from both  both directions um but yeah they all  have like exposed concrete and exposed  steel on the inside  you
 

